NNAAMMEE
     ssooeelliimm — interpret .so requests in manpages

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ssooeelliimm [--CCrrttvv] [--II _d_i_r] [_f_i_l_e _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssooeelliimm utility reads the specified files or the standard input and
     performs the textual inclusion implied by the nroff(1)
     (_p_o_r_t_s_/_t_e_x_t_p_r_o_c_/_g_r_o_f_f) directives of the form:

           .so anotherfile

     If a line starts with: “.so anotherfile” it replaces the line by process‐
     ing “anotherfile”.  Otherwise the line is printed to stdout.

     --CC      Recognise _._s_o when it is not followed by a space character.

     --rr      Compatibility with groff's soelim(1) (does nothing).

     --tt      Compatibility with groff's soelim(1) (does nothing).

     --vv      Compatibility with groff's soelim(1) (does nothing).

     --II _d_i_r  This option specifies directories where ssooeelliimm searches for files
             (both those on the command line and those named in “.so” direc‐
             tive.)  This option may be specified multiple times.  The direc‐
             tories will be searched in the order specified.

     The files are always searched first in the current directory.

     A file specified with an absolute path will be opened directly without
     performing a search.

